OL,3,GNEWSA'We're spending Christmas rowing
OL,4,Athe Atlantic'
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo men will spend Christmas in the
OL,7,Fmiddle of the Atlantic after signing up
OL,8,Fto row 3,000 miles from the Canary
OL,9,FIslands to Antigua.
OL,11,FDuncan Nealon and Daz Ariss, both from
OL,12,FWarwickshire, will take it in turns to
OL,13,Frow continuously for about three months
OL,14,Fin the World's Toughest Row, taking it
OL,15,Fin turns to sleep for a couple of hours
OL,16,Fat a time.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
